## Local Blog Post Frontmatter Template
##
## Copy this file, rename to <slug>.md, and fill in the fields.
## The glob loader only picks up *.md files, so this .example file is ignored.

---
title: "Your Post Title Here (2026)"
slug: your-post-slug
excerpt: "A 150-160 character description with a stat or number for CTR."
feature_image: /images/blog/your-post-slug/hero.png
hero_alt: "Descriptive alt text for the feature image (~125 chars, no 'image of…')"
published_at: 2026-04-19
updated_at: 2026-04-19
status: draft
featured: false
authors:
  - steven
tags:
  - name: AI Recruiting
    slug: ai-recruiting
  - name: Sourcing
    slug: sourcing
canonical_url:                # optional — set to override the default canonical
---

Your markdown content here.

## Section Heading

Regular paragraphs, **bold**, *italic*, [links](https://example.com).

Inline HTML works for tables, SVGs, and charts:

<table>
  <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Pin</th><th>Other</th></tr>
  <tr><td>AI Sourcing</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr>
</table>

Embed an interactive tool:

[tool/boolean-search-generator]

Cross-link to another post (auto-links using the target's title):

[[dice-boolean-search]]

Images from /public/:

![Alt text](/images/blog/your-post-slug/screenshot.png)

## Fields Reference

- title (required) — post title
- slug (required) — URL slug → /blog/<slug>/
- excerpt — meta description for SEO + listing cards
- feature_image — hero image path or URL
- hero_alt — alt text for the feature image (a11y + SEO); omit for decorative images
- published_at (required) — ISO date
- updated_at — last modification date
- status — "published" or "draft" (drafts only show in dev)
- featured — true/false for featured section
- authors — list of author slugs (must exist in Ghost)
- tags — list of {name, slug} objects
- canonical_url — override canonical link (for syndicated posts)
